      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Pretty darn easy.&nbsp; It was all over in under 4 (ish?) rounds.</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Legacy gave lots of extra card plays to Absolute Zero, and thus from round 2 on, Absolute Zero was doing a minimum of 11 points of damage to Apostate.&nbsp; It’s hard for anyone to stand up to that kind of damage.&nbsp; I think AZ put about 2/3rds of the damage on Apostate all by himself.&nbsp; And I think Absolute Zero knocked Apostate down to -7 on his last turn with a great “Frost Bound Drain”/“Coolant Blast” combo.&nbsp; It was also fun to see AZ’s “Cold Snap” destroy the “Runes of Malediction” which brought back the stupid little Imp onto the field, which was then instantly killed by the same “Cold Snap”.&nbsp; Good times.</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">GI Bunker makes destroying the relics no problem.</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Tachyon and Wraith did some assists and some damage, but it really was Absolute Zero’s show.</div>",
